      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Pawnee Pitch",
          "subtitle": "Call Partner Pitch",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Pawnee Pitch is a call-partner Pitch variant. Four players bid for trump; high bidder calls for a partner (by naming a card). Play follows standard Pitch: high, low, jack, game. First team to 10 points wins."
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Pitch descends from the English game All Fours (Seven Up), with bidding added; it became a North American family and social game, especially in the mid-west. Call-partner variants such as Pawnee Pitch allow the high bidder to name a card whose holder becomes their partner (identity hidden until that card is played). The Pawnee name is tied to a ten-point call-your-partner form; rules were contributed by James Adams, whose brothers learned it in Wichita, Kansas in the 1950s; the four-player, ten-point-to-win version is a common variant of that tradition."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Setup",
          "subtitle": "Table, deck, equipment, and deal",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "4. Variable partnerships via call."
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Standard 52 cards."
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "52-card deck."
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "As Pitch: typically 6 each."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Variations",
          "subtitle": "Known ways this game changes",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "list",
              "style": "unordered",
              "items": [
                {
                  "text": "Pass Pitch: Pass cards before bidding."
                },
                {
                  "text": "Smudge: Bid 4 and make all 4 = instant win."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
